# G-DOXYGEN accepted-warning baseline.
#
# One extended-regex per line; blank lines and `#` comments ignored. A doxygen
# warning matching any pattern here is accepted; ANYTHING ELSE fails the gate.
#
# This exists so R1 (verbatim comment fidelity) and "docs build clean" can both
# hold. A warning belongs here ONLY when the text producing it is byte-identical
# to the reference's — i.e. the wart is upstream's and "fixing" it would mean
# editing a faithfully-ported doc comment. Record the reference file and line.
# Any other warning is a rustty defect and must be fixed, not listed.

# `rgb:<red>/<green>/<blue>` in the XParseColor syntax description. doxygen
# parses the placeholders as HTML tags. The text is byte-identical to the
# reference's `include/ghostty/vt/color.h:29-30,305-306` (verified with the
# oracle checkout at 88f57ee66); escaping it in rustty would make the ported
# comment diverge from the source it was ported from.
Unsupported xml/html tag <(red|green|blue)> found
